    {
      "title": "New Mexico court orders Meta to pay $567m over harms to children’s mental health",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/aug/06/new-mexico-court-meta",
      "description": "<p>Ruling comes as part of second phase of landmark trial that found social media company enabled harm against users</p><p>A New Mexico court has ordered Meta, the parent company of Facebook, to pay $567m for mental health harm to children from its platforms.</p><p>Judge Bryan Biedscheid said the bulk of the money – $420m – would be used for treatment services for young people. The rest will go toward awareness and prevention, screening services and other costs over the next five years.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/aug/06/new-mexico-court-meta\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-07T00:22:00"
    },
    {
      "title": "Meta ordered to pay $567 million into abatement fund as remedy to child harms case in New Mexico",
      "link": "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/08/06/meta-to-pay-into-567-million-fund-after-child-harms-case-new-mexico.html",
      "description": "A judge in New Mexico ordered Meta to pay $567 million into an abatement fund after a jury ruled the company violated the state’s unfair practices act.",
      "source_name": "CNBC Top News",
      "published": "2026-08-07T01:28:57"
